1
00:02:31,067 --> 00:02:41,067
All pirates searching for the treasure One Piece must brave the second half of the Grand Line.

2
00:02:41,067 --> 00:02:45,067
These wild and dangerous seas are known as the New World.

3
00:02:45,067 --> 00:02:52,067
Gold Roger and his crew were the only men to ever chart these waters and learn all the secrets they held.

4
00:02:52,067 --> 00:02:58,067
For the rest of the pirates of the world, this has proven to be the end of the road, a graveyard of dreams.

5
00:02:58,067 --> 00:03:09,067
Now, Monkey D. Luffy, a boy whose body became rubber after eating the gum gum fruit, sets sail into the New World with his faithful crew.

6
00:03:09,067 --> 00:03:13,067
I'm gonna be the king of the pirates!

7
00:03:16,067 --> 00:03:24,067
As Luffy and his crew push onto the New World, they make a stop on Fishman Island, where they are pulled into a civil war years in the making.

8
00:03:24,067 --> 00:03:30,067
After meeting with Jinbei, they learn the history of the island and the events that led to their battle with the new Fishman Pirates.

9
00:03:30,067 --> 00:03:37,067
They also learn of Queen Otohime, who despite opposition, fought tirelessly for understanding between humans and fishmen.

10
00:03:37,067 --> 00:03:44,067
If I join Aladdin and the other crew members who do not wish to be pirates, no longer have to be.

11
00:03:44,067 --> 00:03:47,067
They can live in this country without fear of retribution.

12
00:03:47,067 --> 00:03:49,067
It's a way for me to take care of my men.

13
00:03:49,067 --> 00:03:52,067
In case you forgot, Tiger is dead.

14
00:03:52,067 --> 00:03:55,067
I'd love to stay and chat, but we're headed out too.

15
00:03:55,067 --> 00:04:01,067
The Sun Pirates split into three groups, with Arlong, Macro, and myself as captains.

16
00:04:01,067 --> 00:04:06,067
And ever since then, we have continued going our separate ways.

17
00:04:10,067 --> 00:04:14,067
Shaking Fishman Island, a celestial dragon drifts in!

18
00:04:14,067 --> 00:04:25,067
I can't believe we're home!

19
00:04:25,067 --> 00:04:29,067
It's amazing, all right. Never thought I'd live to see this day.

20
00:04:29,067 --> 00:04:36,067
You think back to how much we suffered at the hands of the Celestial Dragons, and it's no surprise we'd given up on ever seeing Fishman Island again.

21
00:04:36,067 --> 00:04:43,067
And if it wasn't for Baz Tai, we'd all still be slaves on Marie Joie, and the nobles would still want to control us.

22
00:04:43,067 --> 00:04:46,067
Being a pirate all these years, well, it was the only way to live.

23
00:04:46,067 --> 00:04:51,067
But here we are, going home to be with our families, and we don't even have to hide.

24
00:04:51,067 --> 00:04:54,067
It's happened! We're finally free!

25
00:04:56,067 --> 00:05:01,067
Hey, Captain. Scratch that. I mean, Brother Jinbei. I'll never forget what you've done for all of us.

26
00:05:01,067 --> 00:05:03,067
Don't get so dramatic on me.

27
00:05:03,067 --> 00:05:06,067
Course not, but we still want you to know that we understand.

28
00:05:06,067 --> 00:05:11,067
The only way pirates like us could truly be free is with the amnesty of the government.

29
00:05:11,067 --> 00:05:13,067
Yeah, and that's why you joined the Warlords, isn't it?

30
00:05:13,067 --> 00:05:16,067
We know that you did it for us, and not because you wanted to.

31
00:05:16,067 --> 00:05:21,067
Alright, that's enough already. If you want to get sentimental, then save it for your families.

32
00:05:21,067 --> 00:05:24,067
Look, they're anxious enough to see you as it is.

33
00:05:24,067 --> 00:05:27,067
Oh, honey. That's Dad?

34
00:05:27,067 --> 00:05:28,067
My love.

35
00:05:28,067 --> 00:05:30,067
Don't worry. Go on.

36
00:05:30,067 --> 00:05:33,067
Dad!

37
00:05:33,067 --> 00:05:35,067
You're home!

38
00:05:39,067 --> 00:05:45,067
Aladdin, after all those years you toiled as a slave, how does it feel to be a free fishman?

39
00:05:45,067 --> 00:05:51,067
Jinbei, as you say, we are free. No longer hunted by the Celestial Dragons, at least.

40
00:05:51,067 --> 00:05:55,067
And at long last, we can return to our families without fear.

41
00:05:55,067 --> 00:06:00,067
But just like the mark of the Celestial Dragons, the agony that we suffered as slaves is seared into our minds.

42
00:06:00,067 --> 00:06:07,067
And though we may walk this world as we please, our hatred towards humans, it will always bind our souls.

43
00:06:07,067 --> 00:06:17,067
To be clear, I understand every word of what Brother Tai tried to impart.

44
00:06:17,067 --> 00:06:21,067
But still...

45
00:06:21,067 --> 00:06:23,067
This makes me sick.

46
00:06:23,067 --> 00:06:27,067
How could Jinbei join up with humans? He's just a tool for the world government.

47
00:06:27,067 --> 00:06:31,067
After everything that happened with them, too. Did he already forget who killed Fisher Tiger?

48
00:06:31,067 --> 00:06:34,067
Hate to say it, but I've lost all respect for him.

49
00:06:37,067 --> 00:06:45,067
I knew quite well what was waiting for me. The Islanders couldn't understand. And they reviled the fact that I joined the Warlords.

50
00:06:45,067 --> 00:07:00,067
I can't imagine a more fortuitous situation. We now have a relationship with the world government thanks to Jinbei.

51
00:07:00,067 --> 00:07:07,067
This is our chance. We can establish friendly relations with humans now. And I will work hard to make sure that we do.

52
00:07:07,067 --> 00:07:14,067
Of course. But while I recognize why Jinbei did it, it troubles me to see him take on such a terrible burden.

53
00:07:14,067 --> 00:07:21,067
If he receives an order from the world government, he'll have no choice but to fight for their cause, regardless of the circumstance.

54
00:07:21,067 --> 00:07:28,067
And no matter how much he might disagree, he will be asked to stand in harm's way and his blood will be spilled.

55
00:07:28,067 --> 00:07:37,067
Yes. He's making a great sacrifice. And I won't let it go to waste. I promise that I'll do my very best.

56
00:07:37,067 --> 00:07:45,067
As long as you also promise me that you won't push yourself too hard, I would loathe to see you suffer another debilitating hangover.

57
00:07:45,067 --> 00:07:57,067
Despite this promising turn of events, something unexpected occurred that would forever alter the path of Queen Otohime's life.

58
00:07:57,067 --> 00:08:01,067
An uninvited visitor arrived on the island.

59
00:08:01,067 --> 00:08:10,067
Ryugu Kingdom, come in! This is the Border Patrol! A large, badly damaged ship is seeking emergency entry into the country!

60
00:08:10,067 --> 00:08:13,067
Well, what are you waiting for? Just do your job and let them in!

61
00:08:13,067 --> 00:08:15,067
It's a little complicated, sir!

62
00:08:15,067 --> 00:08:21,067
It belongs to... a... a Celestial Dragon!

63
00:08:21,067 --> 00:08:25,067
It what?! King Neptune!

64
00:08:25,067 --> 00:08:27,067
Wait, are you sure?

65
00:08:27,067 --> 00:08:31,067
Grant them entry! Send a rescue team right away!

66
00:08:31,067 --> 00:08:33,067
I'll go welcome them myself.

67
00:08:33,067 --> 00:08:35,067
Krino Nohime!

68
00:08:35,067 --> 00:08:40,067
What in the world is a Celestial Dragon doing on the seafloor?

69
00:08:40,067 --> 00:08:45,067
I can't believe this is happening! Must have been attacked by a Sea King or something.

70
00:08:45,067 --> 00:08:51,067
Here's what I don't get. They hate us fishmen, right? So what were they doing sailing through such deep water?

71
00:08:52,067 --> 00:08:55,067
Let's help, you idiots!

72
00:08:56,067 --> 00:09:00,067
My whole worthless crew just had to go and die!

73
00:09:00,067 --> 00:09:04,067
Bring me a mask, you vulgar fishes!

74
00:09:04,067 --> 00:09:08,067
I can't tolerate your fishman stench!

75
00:09:08,067 --> 00:09:13,067
I demand that you bring me a mask!

76
00:09:13,067 --> 00:09:17,067
I need you to save my life! Filthy fools!

77
00:09:17,067 --> 00:09:20,067
This creep's got zero respect for us.

78
00:09:20,067 --> 00:09:23,067
He thinks we're gonna help him talking to us like that?

79
00:09:23,067 --> 00:09:27,067
Doctor, now!

80
00:09:27,067 --> 00:09:30,067
I need help!

81
00:09:30,067 --> 00:09:31,067
Are the medics here?

82
00:09:31,067 --> 00:09:35,067
Well, yeah, they're here, but they're not sure if they want to help that thing.

83
00:09:35,067 --> 00:09:37,067
Put him out of his misery.

84
00:09:39,067 --> 00:09:42,067
He doesn't deserve to live. He's pure scum.

85
00:09:42,067 --> 00:09:45,067
The Seven Warlords are a joke!

86
00:09:45,067 --> 00:09:52,067
I wouldn't sell my soul to take a job working for the world government even if the bastards beg me!

87
00:09:52,067 --> 00:09:55,067
Hell no! You've got way too much integrity, Captain Deakin!

88
00:09:55,067 --> 00:10:00,067
Everyone talks about Jinbei like he's invincible, but he's no match for me as a pirate!

89
00:10:00,067 --> 00:10:03,067
And that much is true, I suspect!

90
00:10:03,067 --> 00:10:06,067
Ba-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho!

91
00:10:06,067 --> 00:10:07,067
Huh?

92
00:10:07,067 --> 00:10:09,067
Sounds like something's going on at the harbor.

93
00:10:09,067 --> 00:10:10,067
Hey!

94
00:10:10,067 --> 00:10:12,067
It's a celestial dragon.

95
00:10:12,067 --> 00:10:14,067
Oh, man.

96
00:10:14,067 --> 00:10:16,067
Looks like a world noble's causing this.

97
00:10:16,067 --> 00:10:18,067
Well, that's interesting.

98
00:10:18,067 --> 00:10:22,067
I guess his ship got wrecked and now he's flipping his lid or something.

99
00:10:22,067 --> 00:10:25,067
Ba-ho-ho-ho! Come on, let's go check it out!

100
00:10:25,067 --> 00:10:28,067
This is guaranteed to be good for a few laughs.

101
00:10:32,067 --> 00:10:35,067
This is not how events were supposed to unfold.

102
00:10:37,067 --> 00:10:40,067
The Fishman slaves have been allowed to return to their island!

103
00:10:40,067 --> 00:10:43,067
How can this be? Daddy dear!

104
00:10:43,067 --> 00:10:45,067
It's bureaucracy, my son.

105
00:10:45,067 --> 00:10:51,067
The Fishman pirate Jinbei joined the Seven Warlords, and he brokered a deal.

106
00:10:51,067 --> 00:10:52,067
But I don't understand!

107
00:10:52,067 --> 00:10:54,067
Jinbei was the captain of the Sun Pirates.

108
00:10:54,067 --> 00:10:57,067
The lowly thugs who've been hiding the slaves.

109
00:10:57,067 --> 00:11:00,067
We negotiated to have their evasion charges dropped,

110
00:11:00,067 --> 00:11:04,067
and obtained amnesty for the slaves to return home, you see.

111
00:11:04,067 --> 00:11:07,067
But if that's the case, then they aren't just any slaves.

112
00:11:07,067 --> 00:11:10,067
Some of them are probably my slaves, right, Daddy dear?

113
00:11:10,067 --> 00:11:12,067
Oh, I'm certain of it, my son.

114
00:11:12,067 --> 00:11:18,067
It turns my stomach to think they're living a free and easy existence after disrespecting us.

115
00:11:18,067 --> 00:11:21,067
Fine then! I'll just have to hunt them down and reclaim them, won't I?

116
00:11:21,067 --> 00:11:26,067
It's only right considering how much money I spent on collecting those slaves in the first place.

117
00:11:26,067 --> 00:11:28,067
Zzzzzzzzzzzzzz.

118
00:11:28,067 --> 00:11:31,067
Hmm, it's not fair. This should be easy.

119
00:11:31,067 --> 00:11:35,067
Why didn't anyone tell me the sea floor was so unhospitable?

120
00:11:35,067 --> 00:11:37,067
Hey! What do you guys think you're doing?

121
00:11:37,067 --> 00:11:39,067
What do you guys think you're doing?

122
00:11:45,067 --> 00:11:46,067
What?

123
00:11:50,067 --> 00:11:52,067
Long time no see, Hamio's guard.

124
00:11:52,067 --> 00:11:55,067
How dare you address me without my title!

125
00:11:55,067 --> 00:12:01,067
Oh! You're all my slaves!

126
00:12:01,067 --> 00:12:03,067
My personal property!

127
00:12:04,067 --> 00:12:06,067
You must return with me at once!

128
00:12:06,067 --> 00:12:09,067
Do you hear? I didn't permit you to run free!

129
00:12:09,067 --> 00:12:19,067
Wait! Don't do it, you guys! He's a celestial dragon!

130
00:12:19,067 --> 00:12:22,067
It'll void the amnesty if you kill him!

131
00:12:23,067 --> 00:12:26,067
Put that gun down! Know your place!

132
00:12:26,067 --> 00:12:29,067
You belong to me and you will do as I say!

133
00:12:29,067 --> 00:12:31,067
I'm your master! Your master!

134
00:12:31,067 --> 00:12:37,067
Up on the surface, all you have to do is cry and the admirals will come running to you at the drop of a hat.

135
00:12:37,067 --> 00:12:40,067
You realize that's the only reason people are scared of you nobles.

136
00:12:41,067 --> 00:12:43,067
But you're at the bottom of the sea floor right now.

137
00:12:44,067 --> 00:12:47,067
As long as the islanders stay quiet, and trust me, they will.

138
00:12:47,067 --> 00:12:50,067
Whatever happens to you, they'll think it was an accident.

139
00:12:51,067 --> 00:12:53,067
Hey, he's got a point there.

140
00:12:54,067 --> 00:12:55,067
I'll keep my mouth shut!

141
00:12:55,067 --> 00:12:57,067
Me too! Mums the one!

142
00:12:57,067 --> 00:12:59,067
Just look at that creep! He's barely even alive!

143
00:12:59,067 --> 00:13:01,067
Might as well get it over with right now!

144
00:13:01,067 --> 00:13:03,067
No! Make it real slow!

145
00:13:03,067 --> 00:13:05,067
He should suffer the same way that you guys did!

146
00:13:05,067 --> 00:13:07,067
Kill him! Make him suffer!

147
00:13:07,067 --> 00:13:09,067
Don't give him any mercy!

148
00:13:09,067 --> 00:13:11,067
What? But why?

149
00:13:11,067 --> 00:13:13,067
I thought everyone respected me.

150
00:13:13,067 --> 00:13:15,067
I can't forgive you.

151
00:13:23,067 --> 00:13:26,067
Not after what you did! Not until my dying day!

152
00:13:26,067 --> 00:13:29,067
No! Don't do it!

153
00:13:29,067 --> 00:13:30,067
Shoot him!

154
00:13:30,067 --> 00:13:32,067
Earn this life!

155
00:13:37,067 --> 00:13:38,067
Don't do it!

156
00:13:38,067 --> 00:13:40,067
You're just stupid fiend!

157
00:13:40,067 --> 00:13:41,067
Kill him!

158
00:13:58,067 --> 00:13:59,067
Kill him!

159
00:14:00,067 --> 00:14:01,067
Kill him!

160
00:14:01,067 --> 00:14:22,067
Oh no, they shot the queen!

161
00:14:31,067 --> 00:14:36,067
Queen Otohime, I...

162
00:14:36,067 --> 00:14:41,067
Everyone, drop your guns at once.

163
00:14:41,067 --> 00:14:44,067
Look around, children are watching.

164
00:14:51,067 --> 00:14:56,067
Aladdin, I heard about the Celestial Dragon. Where is he now?

165
00:14:56,067 --> 00:14:59,067
Not sure, I just got here myself.

166
00:14:59,067 --> 00:15:02,067
Boss Jinbei!

167
00:15:02,067 --> 00:15:05,067
Have you seen our mother? She rushed out of the palace!

168
00:15:05,067 --> 00:15:06,067
To come down here?

169
00:15:06,067 --> 00:15:09,067
Hey brother, these Celestial Dragons, who are they?

170
00:15:09,067 --> 00:15:12,067
They're not like us, they're humans.

171
00:15:12,067 --> 00:15:14,067
Humans?

172
00:15:14,067 --> 00:15:19,067
Not all humans in the world are bad, but these are not to be trusted.

173
00:15:19,067 --> 00:15:23,067
I heard some gunshots right when I got here. Let's go!

174
00:15:23,067 --> 00:15:25,067
Queen Otohime...

175
00:15:25,067 --> 00:15:29,067
It only grazed me.

176
00:15:29,067 --> 00:15:31,067
Why are you protecting him?

177
00:15:31,067 --> 00:15:34,067
You have no idea what kind of pain that man inflicted on us!

178
00:15:36,067 --> 00:15:38,067
The hell he put us all through!

179
00:15:38,067 --> 00:15:41,067
He treated us like we were nothing more than a bunch of animals!

180
00:15:41,067 --> 00:15:42,067
Almost!

181
00:15:42,067 --> 00:15:45,067
I know, I can feel the anguish in your hearts. I do not question that.

182
00:15:47,067 --> 00:15:49,067
Has mother been injured?

183
00:15:49,067 --> 00:15:50,067
Oh no!

184
00:15:50,067 --> 00:16:02,067
I know it's difficult, but you can't pollute the children's minds with your anger towards humans!

185
00:16:02,067 --> 00:16:05,067
Your resentment, do not make it theirs!

186
00:16:05,067 --> 00:16:10,067
They deserve the chance to meet humans and make up their own minds!

187
00:16:16,067 --> 00:16:19,067
Please, you can't tell them!

188
00:16:19,067 --> 00:16:22,067
You have to hold it in!

189
00:16:22,067 --> 00:16:28,067
Our tragedy, and our hatred, they must die with us!

190
00:16:28,067 --> 00:16:30,067
They were one and the same.

191
00:16:42,067 --> 00:16:43,067
No! Watch out, Mother!

192
00:16:46,067 --> 00:16:47,067
You stay still!

193
00:16:47,067 --> 00:16:49,067
Your Majesty! What is this?

194
00:16:49,067 --> 00:16:50,067
Mother, no!

195
00:16:50,067 --> 00:16:51,067
Mother, no!

196
00:16:53,067 --> 00:16:54,067
You bastard!

197
00:16:55,067 --> 00:16:57,067
This stinky fish is your queen?

198
00:16:57,067 --> 00:17:02,067
While a celestial dragon bows before no one, she's just another worthless commoner!

199
00:17:02,067 --> 00:17:04,067
An ignoble bottom feeder!

200
00:17:04,067 --> 00:17:05,067
How dare you!

201
00:17:08,067 --> 00:17:09,067
Can't someone help her?

202
00:17:16,067 --> 00:17:17,067
Now, you fools!

203
00:17:17,067 --> 00:17:18,067
You'll do as I say!

204
00:17:18,067 --> 00:17:19,067
Bring me a mask!

205
00:17:19,067 --> 00:17:20,067
And a doctor!

206
00:17:21,067 --> 00:17:22,067
Because if you don't...

207
00:17:30,067 --> 00:17:31,067
Mama!

208
00:17:35,067 --> 00:17:36,067
What the...

209
00:17:48,067 --> 00:18:00,907
The Sea King!

210
00:18:00,907 --> 00:18:03,407
No!

211
00:18:04,147 --> 00:18:06,407
Oh, oh, oh, oh, oh!

212
00:18:06,407 --> 00:18:07,407
Ah!

213
00:18:07,407 --> 00:18:08,407
Ah!

214
00:18:08,407 --> 00:18:10,407
Ah!

215
00:18:10,407 --> 00:18:11,407
Ah!

216
00:18:11,407 --> 00:18:12,407
Ah!

217
00:18:12,407 --> 00:18:15,407
Ah!

218
00:18:15,407 --> 00:18:16,407
Ah!

219
00:18:16,407 --> 00:18:17,407
Ah!

220
00:18:17,407 --> 00:18:18,407
Ah!

221
00:18:27,407 --> 00:18:29,407
Ah!

222
00:18:29,407 --> 00:18:30,407
What the hell?

223
00:18:30,407 --> 00:18:31,907
It just happened.

224
00:18:31,907 --> 00:18:33,907
That was no coincidence.

225
00:18:38,907 --> 00:18:41,907
Shirohoshi, are you the one who did this?

226
00:18:45,907 --> 00:18:49,907
Wow, Captain, you're really freaking out.

227
00:18:49,907 --> 00:18:52,907
A legend my family spoke of for all those years.

228
00:18:52,907 --> 00:18:55,907
A mermaid gifted with mysterious powers.

229
00:18:55,907 --> 00:18:58,907
An almost supernatural ability that allows her

230
00:18:58,907 --> 00:19:01,407
to summon and control the Sea Kings.

231
00:19:01,407 --> 00:19:04,407
I scoured the sea floor searching for the truth.

232
00:19:04,407 --> 00:19:07,407
Searching for traces of this fabled mermaid.

233
00:19:07,407 --> 00:19:09,407
My family was right!

234
00:19:09,407 --> 00:19:11,407
Their dream was true!

235
00:19:11,407 --> 00:19:12,407
I found her!

236
00:19:12,407 --> 00:19:13,907
I found her!

237
00:19:13,907 --> 00:19:15,907
Wait, you think Shirohoshi's the legendary mermaid?

238
00:19:15,907 --> 00:19:17,907
I knew you'd find her, Captain.

239
00:19:17,907 --> 00:19:18,907
Shush!

240
00:19:18,907 --> 00:19:21,907
No one else can find out about this.

241
00:19:21,907 --> 00:19:24,907
It's a secret legend so old that everyone has forgotten

242
00:19:24,907 --> 00:19:26,907
about it except for my family.

243
00:19:26,907 --> 00:19:28,407
So I suspect.

244
00:19:28,407 --> 00:19:29,407
Can you imagine?

245
00:19:29,407 --> 00:19:32,407
If I could get the Sea Kings to do my bidding,

246
00:19:32,407 --> 00:19:34,407
not a person alive could stop me.

247
00:19:34,407 --> 00:19:37,407
I could do anything and take anything I wanted.

248
00:19:37,407 --> 00:19:38,407
Bah!

249
00:19:38,407 --> 00:19:40,407
So, what's the next step in the plan?

250
00:19:40,407 --> 00:19:43,407
Are we gonna kidnap Princess Shirohoshi or what?

251
00:19:43,407 --> 00:19:44,907
Of course not!

252
00:19:44,907 --> 00:19:46,907
I simply have to make her my wife!

253
00:19:48,907 --> 00:19:51,907
You do realize she's still only a child, don't you?

254
00:19:51,907 --> 00:19:53,907
Yeah...

255
00:19:53,907 --> 00:19:54,907
That's the problem.

256
00:19:57,907 --> 00:19:58,907
Aladdin.

257
00:19:58,907 --> 00:20:04,407
I'll treat him if you wish, my queen.

258
00:20:04,407 --> 00:20:06,407
It's the right thing to do.

259
00:20:06,407 --> 00:20:09,407
I'll take care of your wound next.

260
00:20:09,407 --> 00:20:11,407
A few weeks later,

261
00:20:11,407 --> 00:20:14,407
once the Celestial Dragon's health was stable enough

262
00:20:14,407 --> 00:20:16,407
for him to travel home,

263
00:20:16,407 --> 00:20:18,407
he prepared to disembark for his voyage.

264
00:20:18,407 --> 00:20:21,407
But Queen Otohime did something rather unexpected

265
00:20:21,407 --> 00:20:22,907
before he could leave.

266
00:20:28,907 --> 00:20:36,407
You will pay for this, you damn fish!

267
00:20:36,407 --> 00:20:38,407
You insulted and humiliated me

268
00:20:38,407 --> 00:20:41,407
despite the fact that I'm a respected world noble!

269
00:20:41,407 --> 00:20:43,407
Your actions were unforgivable

270
00:20:43,407 --> 00:20:45,407
and you will come to regret them!

271
00:20:45,407 --> 00:20:47,407
So we just saved his life

272
00:20:47,407 --> 00:20:49,407
and then he turns around and threatens us?

273
00:20:49,407 --> 00:20:52,407
He's got some nerve speaking to us that way.

274
00:20:52,407 --> 00:20:54,407
We provided him with a ship and a crew to go home.

275
00:20:54,407 --> 00:20:56,407
What the hell else does he expect from us?

276
00:20:56,407 --> 00:20:58,407
We shouldn't even be letting him leave anyway.

277
00:20:58,407 --> 00:21:00,907
He's a danger to the whole island.

278
00:21:03,907 --> 00:21:04,907
Wait a minute!

279
00:21:04,907 --> 00:21:05,907
Huh?

280
00:21:05,907 --> 00:21:07,907
It's evident to me that you have more to say.

281
00:21:07,907 --> 00:21:11,907
So I'll travel to the world above with you to hear you out.

282
00:21:11,907 --> 00:21:13,907
She can't!

283
00:21:13,907 --> 00:21:14,907
It's too dangerous!

284
00:21:14,907 --> 00:21:15,907
Please don't go!

285
00:21:15,907 --> 00:21:16,907
Mother, no!

286
00:21:16,907 --> 00:21:18,907
You must reconsider!

287
00:21:18,907 --> 00:21:21,907
I cannot allow you to face such danger

288
00:21:21,907 --> 00:21:23,907
if you truly wish to negotiate with the nobles.

289
00:21:23,907 --> 00:21:25,907
Allow me to go in your place!

290
00:21:25,907 --> 00:21:27,907
I know you'd be safe.

291
00:21:27,907 --> 00:21:29,407
You're the king and a great knight,

292
00:21:29,407 --> 00:21:32,407
so the humans couldn't harm you even if they wanted to.

293
00:21:32,407 --> 00:21:34,407
That's precisely why I should-

294
00:21:34,407 --> 00:21:35,407
You can't!

295
00:21:35,407 --> 00:21:37,407
There's no point in sending a warrior like you.

296
00:21:37,407 --> 00:21:38,407
Hmm?

297
00:21:38,407 --> 00:21:39,407
This is a matter of appearance.

298
00:21:39,407 --> 00:21:43,407
Our nation needs to see that even someone who is as powerless as I

299
00:21:43,407 --> 00:21:46,407
can travel amongst the humans and then safely return home.

300
00:21:46,407 --> 00:21:47,907
That's the point.

301
00:21:47,907 --> 00:21:48,907
Without fear,

302
00:21:48,907 --> 00:21:50,907
and with a heart that's full of trust,

303
00:21:50,907 --> 00:21:51,907
I'll go myself.

304
00:21:51,907 --> 00:21:53,907
That's the only way that this can be done.

305
00:21:53,907 --> 00:21:54,907
Hmm...

306
00:21:54,907 --> 00:21:55,907
Be careful, Mother!

307
00:21:55,907 --> 00:21:56,907
Don't go, Mother!

308
00:21:56,907 --> 00:21:57,907
Don't go, Mother!

309
00:21:57,907 --> 00:21:58,907
Reynaldo Hime!

310
00:21:58,907 --> 00:21:59,907
I can't get it.

311
00:21:59,907 --> 00:22:00,907
Where is she going?

312
00:22:03,907 --> 00:22:04,907
My queen...

313
00:22:04,907 --> 00:22:06,407
Trust in me.

314
00:22:06,407 --> 00:22:09,407
Have faith in the women you married.

315
00:22:09,407 --> 00:22:11,407
And the humans.

316
00:22:15,407 --> 00:22:18,407
You're just the queen of a fish tank!

317
00:22:18,407 --> 00:22:20,407
You arrogant trash!

318
00:22:20,407 --> 00:22:26,907
Goodbye, Mother!

319
00:22:26,907 --> 00:22:30,907
I will miss you!

320
00:22:30,907 --> 00:22:35,907
It's troubling.

321
00:22:35,907 --> 00:22:39,907
Believe me, I know how you feel, but no one can stop her.

322
00:22:39,907 --> 00:22:42,907
All we can do is have faith and hope for the best.

323
00:22:42,907 --> 00:22:44,907
You have to see!

324
00:22:44,907 --> 00:22:47,907
Please be careful up there!

325
00:22:47,907 --> 00:22:50,407
Come home safe!

326
00:22:50,407 --> 00:22:52,407
I love you, Mother!

327
00:22:52,407 --> 00:22:54,407
I love you, Mother!

328
00:22:54,407 --> 00:22:55,407
I love you, Mother!

329
00:22:55,407 --> 00:22:56,407
I love you, Mother!

330
00:22:56,407 --> 00:22:57,407
I love you, Mother!

331
00:22:57,407 --> 00:22:58,407
I love you, Mother!

332
00:22:58,407 --> 00:22:59,407
I love you, Mother!

333
00:22:59,407 --> 00:23:00,407
I love you, Mother!

334
00:23:00,407 --> 00:23:01,407
I love you, Mother!

335
00:23:08,407 --> 00:23:10,407
Otohime returns from the world above

336
00:23:10,407 --> 00:23:12,407
with a ray of hope for Fishman Island.

337
00:23:12,407 --> 00:23:15,407
Her once impossible dream now becomes the dream of her people

338
00:23:15,407 --> 00:23:19,407
as one Islander after another pledges support to her cause.

339
00:23:19,407 --> 00:23:21,907
But just when the path to the future seems to have opened,

340
00:23:21,907 --> 00:23:23,907
a shot echoes through the plaza,

341
00:23:23,907 --> 00:23:25,907
changing the course of history forever.

342
00:23:25,907 --> 00:23:28,407
On the next, One Piece!

343
00:23:28,407 --> 00:23:29,907
A sudden tragedy!

344
00:23:29,907 --> 00:23:31,907
A gunshot shuts down the future!

345
00:23:31,907 --> 00:23:33,907
I'm gonna be king of the pirates!

346
00:23:33,907 --> 00:23:34,907
The pirates!

